The bug was real, and it's fixed: when a turn dies mid-stream, --print now writes the text that had already arrived to stdout and still exits non-zero. Clippy and the full cargo test pass.

Reproducing it (committed as 27d395db, before any change to src/): I gave the local test server a stream that sends the text PARTIAL_ANSWER_7Q and then an overloaded_error event, with no end-of-message event. It sent that same broken stream on every request, and the existing --print -p hi command was left unchanged.
• stdout: "" (empty)
• exit code: 1
• stderr: the error, then (failed after 6 attempts)
• requests: 6 (the first try plus 5 retries)

Why it happened: in src/prompt.rs, the retriable-error result didn't carry the text the dying attempt had received. Once the retries ran out, the retry loop handed back an empty answer, so --print had nothing to print.

Fix (ab076771):
• The retriable-error result now carries that text.
• Both retry loops (text prompts and prompts with images) pass it out when they give up: after the last retry, or when a rate limit is too long to wait for. They use the same path the fatal-error case already uses.
• Only the last attempt's text is kept, so nothing from earlier retries is joined on.
• The exit code stays non-zero and the stderr error is unchanged.

Tests (tests/print_stdout_contract.rs):
• The new test checks stdout equals PARTIAL_ANSWER_7Q exactly, with no trailing newline, the same as a successful --print answer. It also checks the non-zero exit and the stderr error.
• The existing clean-stream tests still pass byte-for-byte, including {"answer": 42}.
• Check that the test actually detects the bug: I made the fix discard the text, and the new test failed by name with left: "". I restored the code in the same command.
• To support this, the test server now counts requests, and there's a variant of the test runner with a longer time limit.

Docs: docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md has a new paragraph: on a mid-stream failure, stdout holds what was produced, and the exit code says the turn failed.

Three things to know:
• **The new test takes about 30 seconds.** That's the real wait between the 6 attempts, since I didn't find a flag to shorten it.
• **--output-format json isn't covered.** It probably also receives the partial text now, because it reads the same answer, but I didn't test it. The docs just say its behaviour here isn't pinned by a test.
• **I didn't add an ARCHITECTURE.md entry for src/prompt.rs.** The task didn't list that file.
